  "prompt": "What did each unit earn during a promotion compared with before it? For each promotion that started in 2025 (start_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025), give the gross margin per unit sold on promotion and per unit sold in the baseline, each rounded to 2 decimals with ROUND. A line's gross margin is its net_revenue_eur minus units times unit_cost_eur. A sales line is on a promotion when it carries that promotion's ID in order_lines.promo_id, whatever its date; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline ends the day before the promotion's start_date and has as many days as the promotion ran, start_date and end_date both counted; it holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale shows its margin per unit as missing. Return three columns, in this order: promo_id, promo_margin_per_unit and baseline_margin_per_unit. Return one row for each such promotion. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "promo_margin_per_unit",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
